		{
			dependencies: ["13186E7B0D6B6115"]
			description: [
				"Well, don't be worried about that."
				""
				"&2Dried Kelp Blocks&r can be compressed to make Coal with the help of an &6active&r Blaze Burner."
				""
				"&7Coal Blocks&r can be compressed to make Diamonds with the help of a &bsuperheated&r Blaze Burner."
				""
				"&aEmeralds&r are renewable from mixing some glass, quartz and some iron in a &bsuperheated&r Blaze Burner."
				""
				"&7Tuff&r can be made from compacting either Gravel or Deepslate in a &bsuperheated&r or &6heated&r &7basin&r with some lava."
				""
				"&9Phantom Membranes&r can be made from &3<wave>haunting</wave>&r &4Rotten Flesh&r."
				""
				"&8Netherite&r is also now renewable with the use of Crushing Wheels by crushing &4Netherrack&r."
				""
				"Netherrack can now be renewed with &cInstant Health II&r potions, fully automated."
				""
				"Go to the next page for bottomless fluids."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Create's Hose Pulleys allow you to pull from a bottomless fluid pit given that it is able to access at least &a10,000&r fluid source blocks."
				""
				"However a &cbug&r exists in Create itself where Hose Pulleys can only output &e10,050&r fluid source blocks before completely failing after &cexceeding&r that threshold."
				""
				"Once that threshold is passed, it will continue trying to output fluid source blocks but it will be immediately obvious on the last layer that it's unable to add any more fluid source blocks."
				""
				"Please take that into consideration when calculating the volume of your pit by &6Length&r x &6Width&r x &6Height&r."
				""
				"All of Finality's molten metals are allowed to be bottomless."
				""
				"Both Condensed Universal Entropy and Order are allowed to be bottomless fluids in addition to Shimmer and Lemonade."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			hide_until_deps_visible: true
			icon: "minecraft:coal_block"
